        "created_at": "2019-02-02T00:06:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PlatinumWarlock\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/48/1869_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> PlatinumWarlock:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In working on my own prototypes, I use a program available on Steam called CardCreator.&nbsp; It costs about $20, is particularly user-friendly, and produces quality finished designs.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That does look interesting. I’ve&nbsp;used Koga’s Illustrator templates in the past, but I don’t know Illustrator so it’s a challenge to not mess it up. :-(&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Does Card Creator have templating available? Or would a new user have to layout SotM cards for themselves?&nbsp;</p>",
